==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Macho Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Mohawk Cat''' when obtained from [[Tiny Meows (Deadly)|Li'l Cat Awakens!]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Although he has overall worse stats than [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], Li'l Cat serves as a meatshield in {{4c}} stages or other such [[Restriction Stage]]s that allow [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]]. His low stats for even a meatshield and slow speed, however, make it one of the worst options, so it is not recommended in line of alternatives.

Li'l Macho Cat also has a Research Effect Up Sm Combo with [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]]. While Li'l Cat won't benefit much from this combo before True Form, others could benefit greatly from this accessible combo to reduce their cooldown times.

==='''True Form'''===
Li'l Mohawk Cat trades part of the spammability, which is a staple in most meatshields, for decreased cost, turning him into the cheapest in the game by a good margin. He can still be used as a meatshield, not differently than any other similar cat, but he becomes a little less effective in exchange for cost, making it a good trade only in money-tight stages. However, his slightly increased recharge time is reduced back to 2 seconds if you use his Combo [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]], which also reduces the recharge times of other Cats, such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]].

==='''Talents'''===
'''Wave Immunity''' is by far the most valuable talent with a wide variety of applications. Most other accessible alternatives can serve as ranged meatshields and [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Glittering Macho Cat]] does the job better, but Li'l Mohawk is arguably the cheapest, both in terms of evolutionary materials and in action.

Giving him a 10% chance to land '''Critical Hits''' can be good for clearing out lesser [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies like [[Metal Doge]] and [[Metal One Horn]], although it should never be seen as a necessity due to his low stats. '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' will rarely be useful because of the aforementioned stat deficiency, and the same can be said for '''Slow Immunity''', as Li'l Cat normally can't survive attacks that inflict Slow.

==='''Orb'''===
Li'l Mohawk isn't a good unit to invest orbs into, any orbs would be better spent on other units.

The Death Mini-Surge ability Orb is the most useful orb, as it can make Li'l Mohawk an actually usable metal peon killer when paired with the Critical talent. Take note that damage increases from the Attack Buff talent are not mitigated by the Mini-Surge's damage decrease. However, it's much more useful to use that orb on a better unit due to his low stats.

A Dodge Attack Orb can help in stalling, but it's rather inconsistent, and only works on every other Li'l Mohawk.
Cannon recharge ability orb is a fairly good option for such a cheap meatshield.

For effect orbs, throw on a Metal Defense Orb if you have any spares. With one he'll be more likely to survive a strike from peons or the odd [[Super Metal Hippoe]], but that's usually where the benefits end.

